e_{\\mathcal E}\\)</span> (binary pairing code)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}universal\\text{-}acceptance\\text{-}language}\\vdash\nA_{\\mathsf{TM},\\mathcal E}\\coloneqq\n\\{\\langle\\ulcorner M\\urcorner_{\\mathcal E},w\\rangle_{\\mathcal E}:\nM\\in\\mathcal D_{\\mathsf{TM}}\\land w\\in\\mathbf 2^*\n\\land\\operatorname{Accept}_M(w)\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}universal\\text{-}acceptance\\text{-}language}\\vdash\nA_{\\mathsf{TM},\\mathcal E}\\coloneqq\n\\{\\langle\\ulcorner M\\urcorner_{\\mathcal E},w\\rangle_{\\mathcal E}:\nM\\in\\mathcal D_{\\mathsf{TM}}\\land w\\in\\mathbf 2^*\n\\land\\operatorname{Accept}_M(w)\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The accepted object is a binary pairing of a valid machine code and an input word; the former ambiguous phrase “<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M(w)\">\\(M(w)\\)</span> Accept” has been replaced by the defined acceptance predicate.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"73-df-binary-program-coding","status":"resolved","id":"db96cabedd089e5f","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-binary-program-coding]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-dtm-language-semantics","status":"resolved","id":"888d8ab66ec7efca","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-dtm-language-semantics]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-binary-program-coding","status":"resolved","id":"db96cabedd089e5f","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathcal E$ with $\\oper